If that's really such a problem for you, have you considered using sounds
to warn you about hunger status? According to the guidebook, the qt and
windows ports support sound, but I think there is a patch to also use sound
in tty.

Something like

SOUND=MESG"*beginning to feel hungry*" "hungry.wav" <volume>
SOUND=MESG"*beginning to feel weak*" "weak.wav" <volume>
SOUND=MESG"*faint from lack of food*" "faint.wav" <volume>

And an appropriate SOUNDDIR. Just a loud, notable "alarm" type sound should
be enough.

